From 961be44a324817bdceb6fae332a60642cdaa52c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:37:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/35] feat: revive Cinebox sprite bokeh with shaped-mask
 intersection (v1)

The CE3-era sprite DOF (technique DofBokehRef, dead code since the
pipeline modernised) lives again as ExecuteSpriteBokeh in the DOF stage,
selected by r_DepthOfFieldMode 0: one self-expanded quad per half-res
pixel, splatting the classic procedural disc+rim - and beyond the
original design, an optional shape TEXTURE (engine ships
EngineAssets/ScreenSpace/bokeh_star/love/music/pentagon/square) that
physically INTERSECTS with the iris polygon: effective aperture = mask
intersected with blades, so stopping down eats the shape back into the
blade polygon. Five latent bugs in the never-compiled shader fixed.

Blade Rotation now turns all three aperture consumers in lockstep -
diffraction streaks, gather kernel polygon, sprite intersection mask -
via the new Dof_User_BladeRotation param.

Two pipeline-order bugs found and fixed on the way, both latent in the
default mode too: motion blur decided "did DOF run?" by re-deriving it
from CDepthOfField::GetParams() - which is NOT pure (it advances a
temporal smoother per call) and was called twice per frame, so MB could
disagree with the DOF stage for exactly one frame on fast aperture
sweeps and composite the pre-DOF sharp frame back over the result in
velocity-tile-shaped stripes. The DOF stage now publishes
HasWrittenHDRTarget() and MB consumes the fact.

Marked v1: the exclusive full-splat mode 0 is preserved here before the
hybrid (gather base + sparse highlight splats) supersedes it - spec in
HybridDofSpec.md.

